  },
  "rows": [
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1029",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Module commands and queries must not read the session themselves. They take the\n    signed-in user as an explicit actor.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1155",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    A user account must not carry a role. Owning and renting come from a user's\n    relationship to rooms and requests.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1290",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Signing up and then signing in creates a session, and resolving the\n    signed-in user from that session's headers returns the user.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1428",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Resolving the signed-in user with no session or an invalid one returns no user,\n    and requireUser then refuses as unauthenticated.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1566",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Submitting a form after clearing the session changes nothing and is refused.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1648",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "cases",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Signing out ends the session, and the next page load redirects to sign-in.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1746",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Identity lets a person sign up, sign in, and sign out with email and password\n    on a user account.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:1852",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Identity provides requireUser, which returns the signed-in user for the current\n    session or refuses as unauthenticated. Every page and action except sign-up and\n    sign-in calls it.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:195",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "state",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Identity owns each *user account*, which has one email and one password\n    credential and no stored role.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:2043",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "interface",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Identity provides resolution of the session from request headers outside\n    Next.js, so the signed-in user can be tested without a running app.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:2211",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "decisions",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Better Auth backs Identity because Auth.js is security-fixes-only and Lucia is\n    deprecated.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:2311",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "decisions",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Roles come from the relationship, not the account, so one person can own and\n    rent without two accounts.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:30",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "goal",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Establish who is acting on every page and action, with one account type and\n    email and password sign-in, so the rest of Slotted never guesses.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:307",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "state",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Identity owns each *session* created at sign-in and ended at sign-out.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:397",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "logic",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    Resolving the *signed-in user* takes four steps. Step one reads the session\n    from the request headers. Step two looks up the user account that the session\n    belongs to. Step three returns the signed-in user, or returns no user when the\n    session is missing or invalid. Step four turns a missing user into an\n    unauthenticated refusal at the requireUser gate, and otherwise hands the\n    signed-in user to the calling page or action.\n"
    },
    {
      "facet": "facet:identity.sigil:864",
      "component": "urn:sigil:component:identity.sigil:Identity",
      "componentLabel": "Identity",
      "section": "constraints",
      "source": "identity.sigil",
      "prose": "    The optimistic redirect on the session cookie is not a security boundary. Only\n    requireUser may decide whether a signed-in user exists for a page or action.\n"
    }
  ],
